course: dictionary
lesson: 6510
title: Neglect: when care goes missing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To neglect something means not giving it the care or attention it needs. «The dust lying thick on everything … the cheerless, deserted look of the long-neglected house» shows you the house has been left alone for a long time. The clues are thick dust, deserted and long, so neglected means left uncared for.
explain: Neglect can be a verb or a noun, and the sentence shows which. «He neglected to tell us» is a verb: it means he forgot or failed to tell us. Test your meaning in the sentence. "He forgot to tell us" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: In school, neglecting homework means not doing it. In safety and law, neglect is much more serious. When parents or carers do not give a child food, safety, warmth or care, this is called child neglect, and adults like teachers must help.
fact: Neglect means not giving enough care or attention to something you should look after.
fact: «Neglected» means left uncared for, as in «the long-neglected house».
fact: «Neglected to» means forgot or failed to do something, as in «He neglected to tell us».
fact: As a noun, neglect means the state of not being cared for, as in «fall into neglect».
fact: Child neglect means a child is not given food, safety, warmth or care, and adults such as teachers must help.
exercise: The Mole sees the «long-neglected house». What does this tell you? | It is full of happy guests | *It has been left uncared for for a long time | It was built last week | It has just been painted bright red
exercise: «He neglected to tell us.» What does neglected mean here? | Wrote it down twice | Shouted the news loudly | *Forgot or failed to do something | Told us very carefully
exercise: Which phrase describes a child who is not given food, warmth or safety? | *Child neglect | Thick dust | Deserted house | Neglected to mention
test: In school, what does neglecting your homework mean? | *Not doing it | Sharing it with a friend | Losing the pencil | Doing it twice to be sure
test: What does «fall into neglect» most likely mean for a garden? | It is painted and new | *It becomes overgrown and broken because nobody cares for it | It is watered every day | It is visited by many guests
exam: Which sentence uses neglect as a verb? | The house was full of neglect | The neglect of the garden was clear to see | *The Mole did not neglect to close the gate | Neglect is a sad word
